## Authentication

The provider authenticates with an email address and an API token:

* **Classic API token** (default): the configuration above.
* **Scoped API token** of a user or a **service account** (Jira Service Management only): set `auth_type = "scoped"`
  (or `ATLASSIAN_OPS_AUTH_TYPE=scoped`); the provider then calls api.atlassian.com for teams and user lookups. A
  `@serviceaccount.atlassian.com` address gets `scoped` by default (service accounts have no classic API token).
* A **user's** scoped API tokens are created per product, so a user needs two of them: `token` with the Jira and JSM
  Operations scopes and `teams_token` (or `ATLASSIAN_OPS_API_TEAMS_TOKEN`) with the Teams scopes. A **service
  account's** token carries all scopes, so it needs only `token`.

{{tffile "examples/provider/provider_scoped_api_token.tf"}}

{{tffile "examples/provider/provider_service_account.tf"}}

The token scopes, service account requirements and limitations are described in the
[Scoped API Tokens and Service Accounts](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/atlassian/atlassian-operations/latest/docs/guides/scoped-api-tokens-and-service-accounts) guide.

